    "xtu_faq_EME89m": {
      "type": "xtu-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "item_BFm6Pq": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I see my dash cam live on my phone?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes! With a True Wireless dash cam like the GKU C600 4G LTE Dash Cam, viewing your dash cam live on your phone is easy. Simply use the dedicated mobile app to access a real-time feed, just like live monitoring. No Wi-Fi hotspot needed - <a href=\"/products/gku-c600-4g-lte-dual-dash-cam\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"GKU C600 4G LTE Dash Cams with Cloud Storage & WiFi 6\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">the C600 uses built-in LTE</span></a><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"> </span>cellular connectivity for true wireless, remote live viewing anytime, anywhere.&nbsp;</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_9gdWxW": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I View My Wireless Dash Cam Remotely?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, if your dash cam supports cellular connectivity and remote live viewing. The GKU C600 supports remote vehicle monitoring through 4G LTE, allowing you to check your car using a compatible app. Remote access requires sufficient power, cellular coverage, and an active data plan.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_AWfwFk": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do Wireless Dash Cams Require a Monthly Subscription?",
            "answer": "<p>Not always. WiFi-based features generally do not require a cellular subscription. However, 4G LTE remote connectivity and certain cloud services may require an active data plan or paid service. Check the specific dash cam's service requirements before purchasing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_FUNbA4": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I Still Use My Dash Cam Without Renewing the 4G Data Plan?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. The GKU C600 can still function as a regular dash cam without an active 4G data plan. You can continue recording driving footage and use the built-in WiFi connection to access videos and adjust settings locally through the app.</p><p>However, 4G-dependent features, such as remote live viewing, cellular GPS tracking, cloud services, and remote parking alerts, will be unavailable until you renew or activate a compatible data plan.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_QqpWkf": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What Is a Wireless Dash Cam?",
            "answer": "<p>A wireless dash cam uses WiFi or cellular connectivity to connect with your smartphone, transfer footage, or enable remote monitoring. Unlike traditional dash cams that rely mainly on physical connections for data access, wireless models offer more convenient connectivity. However, most wireless dash cams still require a power cable.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_6pWPMy": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is a Wireless Dash Cam Better Than a Wired Dash Cam?",
            "answer": "<p>It depends on your needs. A wireless dash cam with WiFi or 4G LTE connectivity offers convenient smartphone access, video downloads, and, on supported models, remote live viewing and parking alerts. A traditional wired dash cam may provide similar recording quality but typically offers fewer wireless connectivity features.</p><p>However, wireless does not mean wire-free. Most wireless dash cams still require a power cable, and front-and-rear systems may also need a cable connecting the rear camera.</p><p>For drivers who want remote vehicle monitoring, the <a href=\"/products/gku-c600-4g-lte-dual-dash-cam\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"GKU C600 4G LTE Dash Cams with Cloud Storage & WiFi 6\"><strong>GKU C600 4G LTE Dash Cam</strong></a> offers built-in 4G LTE connectivity and WiFi 6, combining remote access with convenient local video management.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_YNiUqL": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do wireless dash cams need to be plugged in?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Most wireless dash cams need continuous power from a vehicle's USB port, 12V outlet, or a compatible hardwire kit. Wireless connectivity does not mean the camera operates without power cables.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_di9U4L": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can a wireless dash cam record without WiFi?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Most WiFi-enabled dash cams can record footage to a memory card without an active WiFi connection, provided they have power and suitable storage.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_gKywBY": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can a wireless dash cam work when the car is off?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. GKU C600 supports parking monitoring with &nbsp;hardwire kit included.&nbsp;</p>"
          }
        }
      },
